WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.300
-First off, it's always
great to see you.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.300
-So good to see you.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.334
-Thank you for
playing that game.

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:05.434
And you taught me --
you taught me

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:06.834
a little acting lesson.
-There you go.

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:08.634
-That was it, from the best.
I loved it.

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:09.934
I want to talk
about "Stranger Things."

00:00:09.934 --> 00:00:12.400
-Yeah.
-First half of Season 4,

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.000
Volume 1, premieres May 27th
on Netflix.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:17.934
Everyone's freaking out.

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:20.267
-Yeah.
-I'm so excited.

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:21.767
How would you describe
this season?

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:23.367
What's happening with Eleven?

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:25.501
-My gosh. What isn't happening
with Eleven?

00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:27.901
I think what -- The main part

00:00:27.901 --> 00:00:30.667
and the slogan
of this story line is,

00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:32.467
"It's the beginning of the end."

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:35.467
And we really have to dig deep
into her beginning

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:39.167
and how she became who she is
with the people around her

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:41.834
and how to gain that autonomy

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:44.400
and become this woman
on her own.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.634
So this story line, this season
really digs into that.

00:00:47.634 --> 00:00:49.100
-Yeah, oh, good.
We get some answers?

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:51.501
-Yes, definitely
lots of answers.

00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:52.567
-Yes. I love that, all right.

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:54.467
-Lots of crying,
lots of laughing.

00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:56.501
-I read somewhere that you got
your American accent

00:00:56.501 --> 00:00:57.801
from watching "Hannah Montana."

00:00:57.801 --> 00:00:58.801
-I did. I did.

00:00:58.801 --> 00:01:00.767
-That is true?
-Yes, absolutely!

00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:02.334
-Really?
-Yeah, because I watched

00:01:02.334 --> 00:01:05.067
"Bugsy Malone" and "Godfather"
when I was like 8.

00:01:05.067 --> 00:01:06.801
-I love "Bugsy Malone."
-Yeah, love it.

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:09.734
And I -- You know, my parents
were like, you know,

00:01:09.734 --> 00:01:11.100
watching all these movies
with me.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.267
And I was like, "Yeah, but

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:15.734
'Hannah Montana' is like,
Oscar-nominating.

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:17.567
Like, it's so good."

00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:18.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:20.033
"Hannah Montana's" the best.
-Yeah.

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:22.200
-Like, the film, everything.
-Yeah.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.868
-Everything about it
is amazing.

00:01:23.868 --> 00:01:25.834
And I got the American accent.

00:01:25.834 --> 00:01:26.834
[ American accent ]
So I would always literally

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:27.934
just be like "Hi."

00:01:27.934 --> 00:01:30.734
Like, you know,
"How are you, Jimmy?"

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:32.234
[ Normal voice ]
And then, you know.

00:01:32.234 --> 00:01:34.133
-Do you do, like,
accents when you see them,

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:35.234
like,
when you watch movies?

00:01:35.234 --> 00:01:37.367
-Yeah, I like to --
to see characters,

00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:38.667
and then I just do the accent.

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:40.467
As long as I've watched it
for long enough,

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:43.534
I can kind of get it
to somewhat of a T.

00:01:43.534 --> 00:01:44.834
-Like, what are you
watching now?

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:45.934
-"Inventing Anna."

00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:47.501
-Yes.
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:48.767
-When -- Yeah.

00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:50.567
So, like, I was in
the hotel lobby the other day,

00:01:50.567 --> 00:01:52.634
and they were like "Miss Brown,
we have to run your card again."

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:54.100
I was like [As Anna Delvey]
"Run it again!"

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.400
"It must be your system!"

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:01.300
And it was --
"Why do you look poor?"

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.534
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:05.200
Do you do any other impressions?
-[ Normal voice ] Yeah.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.601
Winona Ryder from Season 1.

00:02:07.601 --> 00:02:08.734
-Oh, "Stranger Things"?
-Yeah.

00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:10.300
Noah and I like to do this one.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.634
Noah's like, "Mom,
I'm in the Upside Down."

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:14.567
And she's like,
"Come on, baby, I am here.

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:17.067
I am coming to find you, honey."

00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:18.934
-Wow!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:21.300
Winona!
I love how you did that.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.667
Noah was just here, by the way.

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:23.934
He was on the show,
and he's great.

00:02:23.934 --> 00:02:25.501
Noah -- Noah Schnapp, hi.

00:02:25.501 --> 00:02:27.100
I know you guys
are best friends.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:28.834
-Yes.
-And he was telling me

00:02:28.834 --> 00:02:30.834
the last night of filming,
I want to say --

00:02:30.834 --> 00:02:31.834
-Yes.
-...that you played

00:02:31.834 --> 00:02:33.901
a pretty big prank on him.
-Yeah.

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:35.701
Well, he's the biggest
prankster of them all.

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:38.067
I, too, am pretty bad.

00:02:38.067 --> 00:02:42.133
But he --
he goes to great extents.

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:45.133
So we thought as a crew
that we needed to get him back.

00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:47.667
So it was 4:00 a.m.
We were in New Mexico.

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:50.200
He was on set, and it was
the last night of shooting.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.167
So we thought,
what better way to get him

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:55.000
than to get him to base camp,

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:00.400
and we had trash bins filled
with water balloons all around,

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.000
and we turned all
the lights off at base camp.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.200
I called him, crying.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.667
"Noah, I'm just so upset
that, you know,

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:08.234
you're not here
to say good-bye to me.

00:03:08.234 --> 00:03:09.400
Please just come back
to base camp.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:10.567
I'm leaving now."

00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:12.501
[ As Noah ] "Okay, Mill,
okay, I'll be there."

00:03:12.501 --> 00:03:14.400
[ Normal voice ]
He gets to base camp.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.567
I'm like, "Noah, I got you
a present," you know.

00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:18.901
And I get him in the middle
of the car park.

00:03:18.901 --> 00:03:22.467
And all of us,
about 20 people, raid him.

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:24.868
Absolutely invade him.

00:03:24.868 --> 00:03:26.467
And it's bad.

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:28.267
But then he -- he got
really aggressive with it.

00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:30.167
He got me on the floor,
Absolutely just --

00:03:30.167 --> 00:03:31.634
I was like,
"My God, I'm a girl."

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:33.734
-[ Laughs ]
-Jesus!

00:03:33.734 --> 00:03:36.133
-We have a video.
Check this out. This is real.

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:39.033
[ Indistinct shouting,
laughter ]

00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:46.634
-How -- How long did that last?

00:03:46.634 --> 00:03:48.100
[ Applause ]

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:49.367
How long did that last?

00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:51.767
-I'm not kidding you,
15 minutes.

00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:54.267
Like, it was the longest video.

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:56.467
It was so insane.

00:03:56.467 --> 00:03:57.901
-Are you worried that
he's gonna get you back?

00:03:57.901 --> 00:04:00.067
-When -- I'm always --
I literally, when I see him,

00:04:00.067 --> 00:04:01.667
I'm like, terrified, you know?

00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:03.701
It's like, one step at a time.

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:05.067
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:07.701
-I know there's a video
you brought of you and Noah

00:04:07.701 --> 00:04:09.734
doing the Fruit by the Foot
challenge.

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:12.067
-Yes.
-Now, what is that exactly?

00:04:12.067 --> 00:04:15.067
-We were on set, really, really
bored, biding time, and thought,

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:18.434
"What better way
to not do school

00:04:18.434 --> 00:04:21.834
and to race each other
with Fruit by the Foot?"

00:04:21.834 --> 00:04:24.234
So you extend the whole
Fruit by the Foot,

00:04:24.234 --> 00:04:26.734
and then you just --
no -- using no hands,

00:04:26.734 --> 00:04:29.400
you have to eat it
as fast as you can.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.033
-We have -- You brought us
this video of that.

00:04:31.033 --> 00:04:32.601
Here's --
-I did.

00:04:32.601 --> 00:04:34.367
-Doing the Fruit by the Foot
challenge.

00:04:34.367 --> 00:04:36.434
-Okay, ready?
Set. Go.

00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:40.234
[ Jimmy laughs ]

00:04:40.234 --> 00:04:43.067
-Wait, look at you!

00:04:43.067 --> 00:04:45.000
Is he gagging?
-Whoa!

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.934
-Yeah, he was almost vomiting.

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:49.601
-Look at you.

00:04:50.601 --> 00:04:53.901
-Oh, that was awful!
-Yes!

00:04:53.901 --> 00:04:54.901
Wow!

00:04:54.901 --> 00:04:57.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:57.734 --> 00:05:01.601
I like the dance at the end,
the victory dance.

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:03.067
That's -- That's pretty good.

00:05:03.067 --> 00:05:04.634
-Yeah, so I bring them
everywhere.

00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:08.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:10.367 --> 00:05:12.133
-You want to challenge me?

00:05:12.133 --> 00:05:13.634
-Yes, because I just think,

00:05:13.634 --> 00:05:15.501
you know,
what better way to leave?

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:17.200
We don't see each other often.
-That's true.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:18.634
-I need to teach you
something else.

00:05:18.634 --> 00:05:21.067
You know, a few acting tips
and [Chuckles] and this.

00:05:21.067 --> 00:05:22.734
-Fruit by the Foot challenge.
You want to challenge me.

00:05:22.734 --> 00:05:25.100
-I do, I do.
It's gonna be great.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.834
I'll see you then.
-I'm very competitive.

00:05:27.834 --> 00:05:29.234
Yeah, you know that.
-Me too.

00:05:29.234 --> 00:05:31.534
Okay, so --
-What do we do?

00:05:31.534 --> 00:05:32.701
-So what you're going to do

00:05:32.701 --> 00:05:35.634
is you're going to extend
the whole thing.

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:36.667
-Mm-hmm.

00:05:36.667 --> 00:05:38.868
-Noah's gonna die
when he sees this.

00:05:38.868 --> 00:05:41.234
By the way, everyone refused
to do it on set with us.

00:05:41.234 --> 00:05:43.033
Like, Finn was like,
"Leave me alone."

00:05:43.033 --> 00:05:44.234
Um, okay.

00:05:44.234 --> 00:05:45.634
Then, what you're gonna do

00:05:45.634 --> 00:05:46.968
is you're gonna take
the paper off.

00:05:46.968 --> 00:05:48.033
-Yeah, okay.

00:05:48.033 --> 00:05:49.300
-Okay, now somebody
in the audience

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:50.667
has to make sure
we're at the same length.

00:05:50.667 --> 00:05:51.968
We don't like a cheater.

00:05:51.968 --> 00:05:54.000
-Oh, that's interesting.
-Okay?

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.400
Put it in your mouth.
-Oh, you put it in your mouth.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:56.801
-Yeah, of course you do.

00:05:56.801 --> 00:05:58.801
Okay.
Are we at the same length?

00:05:58.801 --> 00:05:59.701
-No.
-No.

00:05:59.701 --> 00:06:01.734
-I'm longer, right?
-Yes.

00:06:01.734 --> 00:06:03.634
-Now what do we do?
-Are we --

00:06:03.634 --> 00:06:04.767
Are we good?

00:06:04.767 --> 00:06:06.634
Three, two, one.

00:06:06.634 --> 00:06:08.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:11.234
[ Frantic music plays ]

00:06:11.234 --> 00:06:18.667
♪♪

00:06:18.667 --> 00:06:20.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:20.634 --> 00:06:22.667
[ Bell dings ]

00:06:23.934 --> 00:06:26.100
-The champion! Come on.

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:28.200
Millie Bobby Brown!

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:29.601
How did you do that?

00:06:29.601 --> 00:06:31.267
It's so good.

00:06:31.267 --> 00:06:34.300
-They're so good.
-That's really delicious.

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:35.834
Everyone, I want to
show you a clip.

00:06:35.834 --> 00:06:37.067
[ Light laughter ]

00:06:37.067 --> 00:06:38.501
It's still in my mouth.

00:06:38.501 --> 00:06:40.567
Here's Millie Bobby Brown in
Season 4 of "Stranger Things."

00:06:40.567 --> 00:06:41.567
Take a look.

00:06:42.834 --> 00:06:44.834
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:46.367 --> 00:06:48.367
[ Students murmur ]

00:06:48.367 --> 00:06:51.067
-Whoop. [ Laughs ]

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:55.334
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.334 --> 00:06:56.934
-Oh my God.

00:06:56.934 --> 00:06:59.234
♪♪

00:06:59.234 --> 00:07:03.000
[ Students laughing ]

00:07:04.934 --> 00:07:06.167
-Angela!

00:07:10.501 --> 00:07:12.601
[ Screams ]

00:07:16.133 --> 00:07:17.834
-What the hell was that?

00:07:17.834 --> 00:07:20.567
[ Laughter ]

00:07:22.834 --> 00:07:25.033
-Millie Bobby Brown!

00:07:25.033 --> 00:07:29.067
Season 4 of "Stranger Things"
premieres May 27th on Netflix.

00:07:29.067 --> 00:07:31.133
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show." Stick around.

